{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "toolu_01AusvEQ3RKoK6D8TPWmw7gj", "type": "tool_result", "content": "{\"result\":\"NotificationsAPI depends on nothing within 2 hops.\"}"}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "65663548-01aa-48cb-9cf0-4c9135aa2925", "uuid": "1f4e34ea-f169-4b8e-94f6-ef6c7bf38e41", "timestamp": "2026-11-04T02:20:54.103Z", "tool_use_result": {"content": "{\"result\":\"NotificationsAPI depends on nothing within 2 hops.\"}", "_meta": {"io.modelcontextprotocol/serverInfo": {"name": "project-graph", "version": ""}}, "structuredContent": {"result": "NotificationsAPI depends on nothing within 2 hops."}}, "tool_result_meta": [{"id": "toolu_01AusvEQ3RKoK6D8TPWmw7gj", "permission_decision": {"decision": "accept", "source": "config", "reason_type": "rule"}}]}
{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011Cgh68TMnaXJYcPfNW5xS2", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "ReportingService relies on three services, two APIs and three databases. I queried the graph one hop at a time to see which edge connects each one.\n\n**Dependency tree**\n\n```\nReportingService\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 DEPENDS_ON \u2192 BillingService\n\u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 STORES \u2192 BillingPostgresDatabase\n\u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 CALLS \u2192 NotificationsAPI\n\u2502   \u2514\u2500\u2500 DEPENDS_ON \u2192 OrderService   (also a direct dependency, see below)\n\u2514\u2500\u2500 DEPENDS_ON \u2192 OrderService\n    \u251c\u2500\u2500 STORES \u2192 OrdersPostgresDatabase\n    \u251c\u2500\u2500 CALLS \u2192 PaymentsAPI\n    \u2514\u2500\u2500 DEPENDS_ON \u2192 UserService\n        \u2514\u2500\u2500 STORES \u2192 UsersPostgresDatabase\n```\n\n**Services**\n- **BillingService** is a direct dependency.\n- **OrderService** is reached two ways: ReportingService depends on it directly, and so does BillingService.\n- **UserService** is an indirect dependency, reached through OrderService.\n\n**APIs**\n- BillingService calls **NotificationsAPI**.\n- OrderService calls **PaymentsAPI**.\n- Neither API depends on anything else in the graph (I checked two hops out from each).\n\n**Databases (the end points)**\n- **BillingPostgresDatabase**, used by BillingService\n- **OrdersPostgresDatabase**, used by OrderService\n- **UsersPostgresDatabase**, used by UserService\n\nReportingService doesn't store data in a database of its own. It reaches all three databases through other services. OrderService (and the UserService behind it) is the most important dependency, because ReportingService reaches it two ways. If it goes down, both of ReportingService's direct dependencies are affected.\n\nNo configuration keys are involved. These lookups only follow call, dependency and storage edges, so I didn't trace configuration separately."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 318, "cache_read_input_tokens": 5317, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 318}, "output_tokens": 605, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "65663548-01aa-48cb-9cf0-4c9135aa2925", "uuid": "1847d558-a6d0-47b7-bf54-847d0894ba8b", "timestamp": "2026-11-04T02:21:01.020Z", "request_id": "req_011Cgh68T8eJNmZ3uQNdjiHh"}
